-- License — algebraic license-composition ADT. Eight cases: six nullary
-- (MIT / Apache / GPL / LGPL / BSD / Proprietary) and two with payload
-- (RevShare with a percentage rate + recipients list, and Custom with
-- a free-form terms list).
--
-- Static rows: none. License is a function-internal type — values flow
-- through the composeLicenses / computeEffectiveLicense TS helpers, no
-- JSONB row stores a License instance. Identity registration on the TS
-- side is not needed; the parser-derived Codeable/Labelable defaults
-- from loadFenelModule are sufficient.
--
-- Phase 4a of the ts-elimination workstream — see
-- workstreams/ts-elimination/briefs/phase-4a-license-pilot.md. First
-- per-module entity flip; validates the recipe before scaling to
-- ecom / notion / telegram / closure-construction sweeps.
--
-- `Rate` is extracted as a top-level refined-Number atom for the same
-- reason as profile_tag.fenel's Importance: `|`-refinement is a
-- type-decl-level form only and doesn't parse at field-position type-
-- expr slot. Named-atom extraction (Phase 3c Watch-out §2 path (b)) is
-- the canonical workaround. The named-atom form also gives future
-- consumers of a percentage-bound type a reusable name (a future
-- BookingDiscount or VatRate could share Rate, etc.).
--
-- The pre-4a TS literal used the legacy operator-form predicate
-- `{">=": [...]}` / `{"<=": [...]}` (retired storage-side by migration
-- 0040_operator_form_to_call.sql). Phase 4a rewrites it as
-- `value ∈ [0..100]` — a SetExpr interval refinement, structurally
-- cleaner AND set-algebra-decidable. Same canonical pattern as
-- country.fenel's Latitude / Longitude and profile_tag.fenel's
-- Importance.
--
-- TODO: `recipients: List String` is bug-compatibly preserved from the
-- pre-4a literal. The header comment of the pre-flip TS file said
-- `Profile[]`; the proper shape is `recipients: List EntityRef<"profile">`.
-- That redesign blocks on the wider "RevShare integrates with profile
-- entities" design call.
--
-- TODO: `Custom.terms: List ({})` uses the empty-record `{}` placeholder
-- (AGENTS.md flags `{$record: {fields: []}}` as a documented anti-
-- pattern). The proper shape is `terms: List Term` where Term is a
-- typed-record ADT; out of scope for this pilot.

Rate = Number | value ∈ [0..100]

License = MIT | Apache | GPL | LGPL | BSD | Proprietary | RevShare rate: Rate recipients: List String | Custom terms: List ({})
